<p>
  The fresh build starts from nothing: it clears everything a build regenerates - the
  reference store, the crawl baselines, the error dumps, the harvested examples and the
  suite results - then runs the four suites, harvests the reference and the examples,
  crawls every application, accepts what the crawl stored and verifies it. Thousands of
  fetches, a minute or two; the <a href="?index">overview</a> shows the outcome when it
  lands.
</p>

<p>
  <a href="?build&goBuild=1">Fresh build</a> - there is no undo; everything above is
  regenerated from the applications themselves.
</p>
